/P 203 0 R
/T (The Granger Causality Test is a statistical tool used with time series data . It helps determine if past values of one variable are useful for predicting the future values of another variable. )
/E (The Granger Causality Test is a statistical tool used with time series data . It helps determine if past values of one variable are useful for predicting the future values of another variable. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
485 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 203 0 R
/T (It specifically checks if one time series \(Variable X\) is a good predictor for another time series \(Variable Y\). If Variable X's past values significantly improve the prediction of Variable Y's future values \(better than just using Variable Y's own past\), we say that Variable X "Granger-causes" Variable Y.)
/E (It specifically checks if one time series \(Variable X\) is a good predictor for another time series \(Variable Y\). If Variable X's past values significantly improve the prediction of Variable Y's future values \(better than just using Variable Y's own past\), we say that Variable X "Granger-causes" Variable Y.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
